    "done_when": "In /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/maps/magnetics.json, the evidence string of every corpus-validated differential loop rule whose loop fails the per-shot fit on some vacuum shot names that shot and its slope and r, as decision vacuum-verdict-rule requires. Per the loop-reference fits in docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-loop-reference-rca.html, loops 12, 13, 14 and 27 fail E100595, loops 15 and 16 fail E100579 and E100595, and loop 17 fails E100579; the fragment confirms or corrects this list against that RCA's per-shot table. Only evidence text changes: no target_index, channel_factor, validation_state or other field. The edit is made by a script kept in the run directory, not by hand. The prior magnetics.json is copied first to /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/superseded/pre-verdict-outliers/maps/magnetics.json, and the fragment records both sha256s. A new test in tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py asserts that each of those loop rules' evidence names its failing shots. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset and the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_unit_audit.py. It exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
